# NetworkManager alone manages the network: systemd-networkd stays off. The image disables it, but
# every new install's first boot applies systemd's own presets (the image leaves /etc/machine-id
# out, so each install has a first boot), and 90-systemd.preset turns networkd and its sockets back
# on. Running alongside NetworkManager, its /etc/systemd/network/en.network and eth.network would
# configure any Ethernet connection too. Preset files are read in name order and the first match
# wins, so these lines come before 90-systemd.preset's. Every unit networkd's [Install] section
# names (Also=) is listed, so none is left enabled on its own.
disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-networkd-varlink.socket
disable systemd-networkd-varlink-metrics.socket
disable systemd-networkd-resolve-hook.socket
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
disable systemd-network-generator.service
